          "output": "Recommend a hybrid of X25519 and ML-KEM-768 for TLS 1.3. ML-KEM-768 has a\n~1.2 KB encapsulation key and ~1.1 KB ciphertext, which fits comfortably in a\nTLS handshake. Classic McEliece has a public key around 1 MB, which bloats the\nhandshake and any certificate carrying it and is impractical at e-commerce\nscale. McEliece is more conservative \u2014 code-based, with decades of study \u2014 but\nits key size rules it out for mass TLS. Running the hybrid keeps classical\nsecurity if ML-KEM is later broken while adding quantum security; the added\nbytes are modest.\n"
