          "output": "OpenSSH 9.6 already negotiates post-quantum key exchange by default: since\n9.0 the default has been the hybrid sntrup761x25519-sha512, so your SSH\nsessions are likely already PQ-protected for key agreement. The newer hybrid\nmlkem768x25519-sha256 was added in 9.9 and became the default in 10.0. Hybrid\nmeans the session is secure if either X25519 or the PQ algorithm holds.\nRecommended action: upgrade toward 10.x and verify with `ssh -Q kex` and your\nKexAlgorithms config. Note 10.1 warns when a non-PQ key exchange is selected.\n"
