          "status": "call",
          "output": "The two halves of TLS moved at different speeds. Key exchange is deployed:\nbrowsers and CDNs negotiate the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 (codepoint 0x11ec),\nwhich protects against harvest-now-decrypt-later. Signatures are not: PQ\ncertificates are rare because of size, PKI and root-store hurdles, so\nauthentication still relies on classical ECC/RSA. Key exchange protects\nconfidentiality of captured traffic; signatures protect authentication now.\nThe gap means your sessions are confidential against future decryption but\nstill authenticated classically. Plan for PQ certificates and crypto-agility.\n"
        }
