          "output": "CNSA 2.0 requires LMS or XMSS per NIST SP 800-208 for software and firmware\nsigning. These are stateful hash-based signatures: each one-time key index\nmust be used exactly once, so the signing system must reliably track and never\nreuse state. That constraint is why signing is expected to run in hardware\n(HSM) and is a poor fit for a large, distributed set of signers. By contrast\nML-DSA and SLH-DSA are stateless. CNSA 2.0 targets exclusive use of these\nsigning algorithms by 2030 (support and prefer by 2025).\n"
